cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these kits in your work, please cite them as below."
title: "SME Cyber Resilience Accelerator"
abstract: >-
  Three independently adoptable reference kits — Identity and MFA, Logging and
  Alerts, and Backup and Recovery Drills — that help small and mid-sized
  organizations and the teams that support them implement strong
  authentication, central logging with alerting, and verified recovery on
  common web-application stacks, with automated acceptance checks and a
  control-to-evidence checklist mapped to NIST CSF 2.0.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Yarovoy
    given-names: Alexander
repository-code: "https://github.com/alex-yarovoy/sme-cyber-resilience-accelerator"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
keywords:
  - cybersecurity
  - cyber resilience
  - small business
  - multifactor authentication
  - logging
  - alerting
  - backup
  - disaster recovery
  - NIST CSF 2.0
